[h1]Flavorium Universalis[/h1]

[b]Compatible with EU5 1.3.* BETA | Multiplayer synchronized[/b]

[hr][/hr]

Workshop can't fit the whole description [url=https://wtmenten.github.io/flavorium-universalis]find it here[/url] along with my age-branch advances planner tool.
[h2]Overview[/h2]

[i]Early preview — mod is stable through 1800s but some systems (large late-game subjects, bond chains, Mexico situation) are less tested. Balance subject to change.[/i]

Flavorium Universalis enhances vanilla EU5 across cabinet gameplay, subject diplomacy, AI behavior, and historical flavor:
[list]
[*] [b]Dynamic AI Personalities[/b] — 27 historically-informed arcs that evolve across the ages; context-driven drift for all AI countries
[*] [b]Cabinet Members[/b] — traits, rivalries, duties, stepping-stone progression, war council events, colonial postings, lasting legacies
[*] [b]18 New Subject Types[/b] — Shadow States, Client States, Palatinates, Chartered Companies, Military Marches, and more
[*] [b]Protectorate & Holy Protectorate Event Chains[/b] — ward maturation → vassal, diplomatic incident escalation, faith crises, religion divergence, and Papal interactions across 9 new events
[*] [b]Overlord-Subject Bonds[/b] — five-dimension relationship tracking with Age of Revolutions payoff events
[*] [b]70+ Era Advances[/b] — subject unlocks, literacy chains, confessional trees, colonial doctrine across all ages
[*] [b]Frontier Governance[/b] — a lesser Frontier Governor for rural, road-less interior provinces (steppe, mountains, the Mandate of Heaven), with a branch-independent advance and four per-estate frontier privileges
[*] [b]Invasion of Mexico[/b] — Mesoamerican Confederation IO, Expedition CB, 28+ conquest events
[*] [b]Balance of Power[/b] — two-pole great-power situation (Preponderant Bloc vs. Balancing Coalition), Preponderance Share, Napoleonic-era warfare/economy/diplomacy events, player actions to petition/leave a bloc or spend bloc Ambition/Resolve as its leader, four endings incl. a Concert of Europe
[*] [b]Hundred Years War Flavor[/b] — starting modifiers, war outcome stacking, vassal defection pressure
[*] [b]Literacy Rebalance[/b] — regional differentiation, library rework, regional catch-up advances
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Cabinet System[/h2]

Ministers accumulate [b]144+ traits[/b] through events — Core (24), Age (36), Conditional (75), Negative (9) — and interact with each other, your realm, and foreign courts.

[b]Cabinet Duties[/b] — assign ministers to War Council, Domestic Reform, Diplomatic Mission, Scholarly Inquiry, Religious Oversight, or Colonial Posting for ongoing modifiers and boosted event chains.

[b]Stepping Stone Chains[/b] — ministers start as fumbling reformists or green adjutants and advance into specialists over a lifespan. Matching duty assignment doubles progression rate.

[b]Court Rivalry & Cabal[/b] — opposing ideologues build tension through a three-stage rivalry chain (Complaint → Letter Unsealed → Faction Hardens). Aligned ministers form cabals and push joint agendas.

[b]Cabinet Composition[/b] — aggregate auto-modifiers activate when your court matches a profile: Warlord Court, Merchant Republic Spirit, Enlightened Court, Court Paralysis, Estate Faction Capture, and more.

[b]War Council[/b] — military ministers drive events during wars; post-war reform proposals unlock after victories.

[b]Synergies[/b] — 26 standard trait-pair synergies, 10 dual-role synergies, 12 cross-court synergy events.

[b]Legacies[/b] — legendary ministers (Grand Vizier, Tribune, Philosopher King) leave permanent country modifiers on death.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Subject Types (18)[/h2]

[b]Personal Union:[/b] Junior Partner, Lesser Partner
[b]Shadow/Client:[/b] Shadow State, Client State, Puppet State
[b]Elite & Cultural:[/b] Elite Enclave, Palatinate, Artists' Commune, Scientific College, Naval Administration
[b]Trade:[/b] Associated Republic, Chartered Company
[b]Governance:[/b] Protectorate, Crown Dependency, Holy Protectorate (Age 4 only, blocked in Age 5+), Provincial Governorate, Tax Farm, Military March

Some require matching estate privileges or government reforms. A five-dimension bond system (economic, military, political, cultural, personal) tracks long-term relationships, with Age of Revolutions payoff events reflecting how you treated your subjects.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Dynamic AI Personalities[/h2]

AI countries evolve their grand strategy across the ages. [b]27 countries[/b] have historically-grounded arcs (TUR, FRA, ENG, MOS, CAS, HAB, POR, SWE, POL, LIT, DAN, BUR, VEN, PAP, GEN, BYZ, HUN, MAM, ETH, MNG, SHO, KOR, NOG/GLH, NAP, SCO, MLO, MLI/SON).

Key inflection events at historical turning points — the Conquering Sultan, Ottoman Stagnation, Sun King Rises, Britannia's Maritime Empire, and more — let AI countries choose between the historical path and alternatives. A post-event guard prevents random drift from overriding assignments for ~20 years.

[b]Game rule modes:[/b] Vanilla, Dynamic Historical, Dynamic Drift Only, Dynamic Historical + Drift (default).

